WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.668
The goal today by Hunter

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:02.235
Biden's team

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.104
was to keep the Republicans guessing,

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:04.938
and he did

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.474
right up to the moment he walked up these

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.975
these steps here

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.044
and delivered that very forceful,

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.579
that very defiant statement

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.515
that you heard just a part of just now

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:19.019
really answering for the first time in in

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.754
the best way he could.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:21.488
Some of the questions

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.956
that Republicans have been having,

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.524
throwing his way,

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.792
essentially the statement

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.627
that he was probably going to be able

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.862
to read

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:32.065
to Republicans if he had sat for that

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.366
closed door deposition.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.200
Instead,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.202
he said he preferred to do

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.038
a public hearing

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.305
and so he showed up here

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.340
on the Senate side.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.808
The Republicans were sitting

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.476
over on the House side.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.577
He showed up here

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.713
at what is called the Senate swamp

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.048
to deliver that statement.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.783
A lot of it was very, very personal,

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.951
talking about his personal struggles,

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.420
struggles with addiction,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.355
and also defending his father,

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.689
defending the fact that he says

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.324
that there is no evidence to indicate

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.426
or to show

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.260
that his father

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.561
benefited financially

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.330
from any of his very messy

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.565
financial dealings.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.599
Those financial dealings

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.868
he got paid millions of dollars

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.103
working with a company

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.338
in Ukraine, one in China.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:12.672
Of course,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.506
that's one reason

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.974
why this this inquiry

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.109
has been ongoing for now

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.510
for over five years.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.945
And, of course, John,

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:19.746
what makes this

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.014
even more complicated for Hunter

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:21.815
Biden is that,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:22.115
you know,

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.216
just in the time

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:23.950
since

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.820
the Republicans sent him that subpoena,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.488
since since that time,

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.091
he has been indicted

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.025
with tax

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.593
charges in California,

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.229
where he is now facing two trials. Right.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.498
One for tax charges in California,

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.199
another one

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.067
for possessing a gun

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.469
during the time that he was

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.403
addicted to drugs

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:44.771
and should not have been able

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.673
to possess one in Delaware.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:47.841
So now

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:48.675
this is now

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.276
a political problem, obviously,

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.445
for the Biden campaign.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.114
And Republicans have threatened

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:54.881
that they are going

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.416
to hold him in contempt.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:57.584
And so now it's

00:01:57.584 --> 00:02:00.487
up to them to see what they do next.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:00.854
John.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:02.922
Evan Perez for us on Capitol Hill.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.290
Evan, thanks so much.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:04.657
All right.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.892
Let's now go to Manu Raju,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:06.659
who is on Capitol

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.727
Hill, as usual,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.829
chasing after reaction

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.631
in this case from Republicans.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.398
What are you hearing?

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.268
I know we heard from James Comer,

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.736
who was trying to explain why

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.238
this was happening in the first place.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:22.008
What are you hearing there?

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:22.408
Yeah,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.009
James coming to the

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.010
House Oversight Committee

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.411
chairman, making clear

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.881
that he wants a private deposition

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:30.150
with Hunter Biden and that eventually

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.651
they'd be willing to have him in public.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.886
But they say the way the

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.120
investigation is going,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.022
people need to be deposed first

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.457
and then there can be a public hearing.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.958
They are threatening to hold him

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.994
in contempt of the House

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:43.830
for not appearing behind closed doors.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.832
We expect that process

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.299
to play out

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.834
over a matter of several weeks.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.836
So this could be punted into next year

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.638
as Hunter Biden defies a subpoena.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:52.705
Now, I also caught up

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.706
with a number of Republicans

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.308
on the Senate side of the Capitol,

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.676
including several of them

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.577
who have been involved

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:59.045
in the Hunter Biden matter,

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.246
some of them investigating

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:02.148
Hunter Biden's alleged ties

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.249
with his father

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.285
over his business dealings and the like.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:07.820
And they made clear that they

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.355
they believe that Hunter Biden

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.857
has a right to make a statement,

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.225
but they also believe that

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:16.863
he should say it under oath.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.131
Hunter Biden just made a

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.600
statement here saying that he has done

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.201
nothing wrong.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.369
Republicans have attacked and distorted

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.238
the truth about his family as president,

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:25.805
and his father

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.040
was not financially involved

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.374
with his business dealings.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.043
He's willing to testify in public.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.578
What do you say to him?

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:32.045
You know,

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.147
he has a right to make a statement.

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.415
And I think some of the facts

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.116
probably are contrary to what he says.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.986
But the main thing is to have a process.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:40.587
You know, his being

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:41.788
and that is, if I were him,

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.990
I'd be reluctant to say anything.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.225
He said that he has.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:45.992
His father

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:46.960
was not

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.161
financially involved

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.797
in any way with his business.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.865
Do you accept that?

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:56.135
I'm going to take the same position

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:59.305
I've taken since I came, that

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.575
all I can say is there's some indication

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.678
of maybe some compromise

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.548
with China particularly,

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.783
but I have no evidence of it.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.252
I'm going to just follow the facts

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.386
where they are

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.053
and the facts

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.089
haven't taken me to that point

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.390
where I can say

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:23.496
that the president is guilty of anything.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:24.931
Now, this comes as the House

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.733
is planning to have a vote tonight

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.600
to authorize

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.236
an impeachment inquiry into Joe Biden,

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:31.838
even as many Republicans

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:32.605
will acknowledge,

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.107
they have yet to prove

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.341
that Joe Biden acted

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.210
corruptly to aid his son

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.978
in any way with those overseas

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:39.846
business dealings.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:40.813
But Republicans

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:41.547
are planning to vote for it,

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.016
even the ones who are skeptical

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.351
because they say they need more power

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.287
to find the evidence

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.689
to actually go to court if they have to

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:50.290
and the like.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.058
So we do expect that vote to happen

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:52.692
this evening.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.193
But actually getting to the point

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.395
of impeaching the president,

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:56.996
a completely separate matter.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.198
A lot of those vulnerable Republicans,

00:04:59.198 --> 00:04:59.799
in particular

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.267
ones from swing districts,

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.802
are uncertain about whether or not

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.537
they will go to that length

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.039
to impeach the president, making him

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:06.906
just the fourth

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:07.774
in American history

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:09.342
to go down that route.

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:10.476
But at the moment, at the least,

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.144
the investigation

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.845
nation plans to go ahead as they weigh

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.514
the next steps with Hunter Biden's

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.883
defiance of the subpoena as well.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:17.216
Manu?

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.384
Roger, we are in strange

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.552
and unprecedented times.

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.821
Thank you so much for all your reporting.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:22.588
Joining us now

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.023
is former Republican congressman

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.591
and CNN senior political commentator

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.326
Adam Kinzinger.

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:27.093
He also served,

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:29.028
of course, on the January six

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.530
congressional committee.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.800
What did you think of Hunter Biden today?

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.535
You.

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.503
I mean, I thought politically and like

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.872
message wise, it was a brilliant move.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.307
I mean, they have made it clear

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.008
that they're willing

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.710
to testify in public.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.778
You know, I think Manu in his report

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.647
said some of the senators were saying,

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:48.214
well, it's great

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.349
he needs to do it under oath.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.183
Well, he can do that

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:51.517
under oath in public.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.353
He has made it clear,

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.021
I think his concern is, look,

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.656
when we go behind closed doors,

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:58.624
the Republicans in the House

00:05:58.624 --> 00:05:59.659
have already made it clear

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.327
they've deemed him guilty.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.696
They've deemed the president guilty

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:05.365
on no evidence, as they've said.

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:06.032
No evidence.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:06.332
This.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.201
Tonight, this vote tonight

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.402
potentially for an impeachment

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:11.704
inquiry will be the first time

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.573
in American history

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:15.608
that they're using an impeachment inquiry

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.909
not to get to,

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.212
you know, justice has it hesitate,

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:20.646
but we have to get to justice.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:21.848
But as a way to go

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.182
on a fishing expedition,

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.385
you're going to have all day on CNN,

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:27.120
these so-called moderate Republicans

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.988
come on and talk about how, boy,

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.123
they don't know if he's guilty,

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.457
but they have to do this

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:32.191
so they can get to

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.593
the answer of some things.

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:35.128
This is the first time in history

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:35.828
that will happen.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:36.629
And a lot of them

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:37.663
are going to take that approach

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:38.798
because they want to satisfy

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.566
the market base at the moment

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.235
and vote for the impeachment inquiry

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:43.836
while trying to look reasonable

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.138
and and truly like,

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.272
oh, we're all for justice.

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.573
This is look,

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:49.008
if you have evidence

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:52.879
of the president having

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.248
this impeachment inquiry and impeach him,

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:57.383
but they don't have maps of that

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:58.918
and they're desperate to find it

00:06:58.918 --> 00:06:59.685
because they have

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.387
determined the outcome

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:03.523
before they've even gotten the facts.

00:07:03.523 --> 00:07:04.424
So a couple of things on that.

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:05.124
We heard from.

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:07.326
We've heard Republicans

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.795
speak out after Hunter

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.630
Biden made his comments.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:11.497
They're not happy.

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:12.432
They're not going to

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:15.234
stop their investigation, as we know.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:16.569
One thing we heard

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:18.638
from Judiciary Committee

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:21.007
Chairman Jim Jordan is this.

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:21.741
He said,

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:24.744
when Congress asks you to come testify,

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.946
you are supposed to come testify.

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.748
And as someone

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.016
who served on the committee,

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:31.584
who issued a subpoena to Jim Jordan,

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:33.286
which he defied,

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:34.320
what are people

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.057
supposed to take from this?

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.158
Well, they're supposed to take that

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:41.127
Jim Jordan is an absolute hypocrite.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.428
Jim Jordan

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:44.497
in front of the Rules Committee

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.364
when we were talking

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.732
about holding

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.368
the Steve Bannon or somebody in contempt,

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:50.470
he said in front of the Rules

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.505
Committee that the Department of Justice

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:53.706
and the FBI

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:54.807
should be the ones

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:56.742
investigating Donald Trump

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:58.077
and that would be their role.

00:07:58.077 --> 00:07:59.045
Now, of course, he's

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.613
against the Department of Justice

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:02.982
in the FBI investigating Donald Trump.

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.317
He's for the,

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:04.617
you know,

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:08.287
sanctity of the of the subpoena by the US

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:09.455
Congress until he's

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:10.556
the one that gets subpoenaed

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:11.557
by US Congress.

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:13.292
And he also votes against

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:14.660
enforcing subpoenas

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.229
against people like Steve

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:17.997
Bannon and against people like

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:18.764
Mark Meadows.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:19.665
I mean, this is

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:22.168
the hypocrisy is mind numbing.

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.736
I am less concerned

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:25.104
with what people's view

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:26.372
is on positions

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:29.375
and what their idea is on policy.

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:30.843
As much as I am with

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:34.013
there is just open and blatant

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:36.649
and unashamed hypocrisy

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.317
where it's all about winning.

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.720
It's all about power and truth

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.621
and justice

00:08:41.621 --> 00:08:43.756
really has no role in what they're doing.

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:46.759
If you have evidence that Joe Biden,

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:47.827
not Hunter Biden,

00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:49.929
but that Joe Biden broke the law,

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:50.863
bring it forward.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.298
And if it's impeachable, impeachable,

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.966
but you don't have that evidence.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:56.068
So you go on a fishing expedition

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:56.836
and all of a sudden

00:08:56.836 --> 00:08:58.504
you raise the flame of justice

00:08:58.504 --> 00:08:59.138
in Congress

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:00.373
like you're so concerned

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:02.108
with the congressional subpoena

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:03.676
when you were the one that ignored it

00:09:03.676 --> 00:09:05.044
the whole time

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:05.811
on this vote

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.079
that's coming to kind of to

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:10.049
formalize the impeachment inquiry.

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:11.784
Tom Emmer is the majority whip.

00:09:11.784 --> 00:09:13.452
He said he probably said it.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:14.287
We heard it from a few people.

00:09:14.287 --> 00:09:15.354
He said probably most clearly

00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:15.922
to reporters

00:09:15.922 --> 00:09:17.523
Voting in favor of an impeachment

00:09:17.523 --> 00:09:22.028
inquiry does not equal impeachment.

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:23.529
Do you think there is

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:27.500
a scenario where this inquiry is launched

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.168
and it doesn't end

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:30.369
in articles of impeachment

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:33.372
against Joe Biden?

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:35.174
Look, if I was in Vegas betting,

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:37.143
I would put all of my money

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:38.077
on no matter what,

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:39.245
this ends in impeachment.

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:40.346
And I said this at the beginning

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:41.113
of the year.

00:09:41.113 --> 00:09:42.048
Keep in mind, Marjorie

00:09:42.048 --> 00:09:42.949
Taylor GREENE, who's

00:09:42.949 --> 00:09:45.117
now the de facto head of the GOP,

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:46.819
introduced articles of impeachment

00:09:46.819 --> 00:09:47.620
on Joe Biden,

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:48.921
his first day in office

00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:50.022
before anything

00:09:50.022 --> 00:09:51.824
was even accused or known.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:53.693
So they've made it clear

00:09:53.693 --> 00:09:55.094
that they have to impeach him.

00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:56.996
The base is demanding that,

00:09:56.996 --> 00:09:58.864
which is why people like Tom Emmer

00:09:58.864 --> 00:10:00.666
and all these so-called moderates

00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:02.201
are voting for this inquiry

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:04.537
because they think and this is a mistake,

00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:06.305
you know, everybody made in Congress

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.540
my whole time there.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.308
You think if you give the MAGA base

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:10.209
a little bit,

00:10:10.209 --> 00:10:11.410
they're going to kind of lay off

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.746
you and then you can go on other news

00:10:13.746 --> 00:10:15.615
channels and look reasonable, like,

00:10:15.615 --> 00:10:17.550
Oh, I'm not sure we need to impeach.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.119
No, you are enabling the inevitable

00:10:20.119 --> 00:10:21.220
impeachment of Joe Biden

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.688
potentially based on nothing.

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:24.457
If you come up with evidence, fine.

00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:25.291
But right now

00:10:25.291 --> 00:10:26.826
you don't have that evidence

00:10:26.826 --> 00:10:27.860
and you're going to move forward

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:28.594
with impeachment.

00:10:28.594 --> 00:10:29.729
Have no doubt

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:30.529
an impeachment

00:10:30.529 --> 00:10:32.765
inquiry is the beginning of impeachment.

00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:34.066
It's not just some,

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:36.102
you know, desire to get to the truth.

